s","/farmland-atlas/kansas/barber-county"],["ARC or PLC in Barber County","/arc-plc/kansas/barber-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 41 of those 75 years. In 2025, February to March came in at 22% of normal and August to September at 165% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 32% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 20224 had its driest year in 1954 at 44%.</p>"}
